### Churchit self-hosting settings ###

## Automatic Configuration ##
# This file should only need to be modified if manually configuring the installation
# of Churchit. If you are running the automatic setup scripts, the `.env` file will
# be auto-populated on the first run.

## Manual Configuration ##
# For manual configuration (if not using the automatic setup scripts:
# Copy this file to ".env" and adjust as needed.

# Your church's domain. It must have a DNS "A record" pointing at this
# server's public IP so Caddy can fetch a free HTTPS certificate.
# For local-only use or for evaluation purposes, use: churchit.localhost
SITE_NAME=churchit.localhost

# Address Caddy answers on. Leave blank to reuse SITE_NAME with automatic HTTPS.
# For a local test with NO browser certificate warning, set the http:// form,
# e.g.  CADDY_ADDRESS=http://churchit.localhost
CADDY_ADDRESS=

# Passwords. Make SURE they are secure!
DB_ROOT_PASSWORD=change-this-db-password
ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-this-admin-password

# Prebuilt image from GitHub Container Registry.
IMAGE=ghcr.io/meichthys/churchit
# Edit the tag below if you want to prevent auto-updating to the latest version
# You can choose from the available tags on the github container registry
TAG=latest
